ghpull:760 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "docs: config/command-language strategy recommendation" ;
    bl:number 760 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:420 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr760 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:420 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-10-31T16:04:52Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-31T16:04:52Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr760Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #420 consolidated #233 (developer-story-driven research into whether dagalog should adopt a Fuseki-style declarative config language, an RDFox-style imperative command language, or something else for setup/administration) and #401 (equinor/Dexpi2Imf's concrete complaint: ad hoc .sh wrappers around fixed --data/--ontology/--rules/--serve flag combinations, duplicated and drifting across scenarios, not portable to Windows). Wrote up the four #233 personas as concrete scenarios against dagalog's actual code (src/main.rs's Cli flags, sparql_endpoint's admin/dataset-scoped HTTP routes, the dagalog-kernel Jupyter cell-magic scripting hook) rather than from memory -- a sibling plan-doc agent in this session had already had to redo work after citing unverified spec details, so every claim here was checked against the source file and line, and the Dexpi2Imf scripts were fetched and read verbatim (not summarized) after an advisor review caught that a first pass had paraphrased the siblings incorrectly from a lossy fetch summary. That verbatim read also surfaced that none of the three scripts actually gets a working one-shot query mode from appending --query to \"$@\" (--serve is already baked into the exec line and wins), which became a concrete design constraint rather than an assumption." ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr760Decision ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:760 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr760 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr760Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Recommended a declarative TOML startup config file (direction 1): named profiles select a set of ontology/rules/data/mapping/ottr inputs, with a shared-inputs-or-inheritance composition mechanism so the ontology list Dexpi2Imf's three scripts all repeat gets written once, not duplicated per profile in TOML the way it's duplicated per .sh file today. Scoped v1 narrowly to one profile targeting the single implicit default dataset (matching every real Dexpi2Imf script and persona 1d), explicitly deferring multi-dataset-at-startup provisioning since nothing in the evidence needs it yet and it would require new sparql_endpoint registry/reasoner-seeding work, not just CLI parsing. Kept today's 'reload every start' persistence semantics (confirmed via serve_on_listener/QuadChangelog::replay_into, which layers the changelog on top of freshly-reloaded --data files) rather than inventing new seed-once semantics nothing currently demands." ;
    agp:alternative "Rejected an RDFox-style imperative command/script language (direction 2) as the primary recommendation: it subsumes directions 1 and 3 but at a much larger grammar/interpreter/test-suite cost, for a payoff the existing admin API (POST /$/datasets, /{name}/data, /{name}/rules, /{name}/rml, /{name}/ottr, /transaction/*) already delivers for every runtime operation except two confirmed gaps -- no runtime OWL-ontology-loading endpoint for any dataset (filed as #759, sub-issue of #420, Status Todo), and no multi-dataset creation shortcut. Also considered a thin client-side tool replaying a config file as HTTP admin-API calls (direction 3) as the lowest-cost option, but rejected it as the *primary* recommendation because it structurally cannot drive one-shot query mode (--data ... --query ..., no --serve), which has no HTTP surface to replay against; kept it as a plausible follow-up layered on the same TOML format instead." .
